ἀπ-έχω, [  [in LXX chiefly for רחק;] ]    1. . trans.,    (a) . to hold back, keep off;
    (b) . to have in full, to have received (on the &amp;quot;punctiliar&amp;quot; force of the compound, v. M, Pr., 109, 247): c. acc., Mt 6:2, 5, 16, Lk 6:24, Phl 4:18, Phm 15 (for illustr. from π., where it is used in receipts, v. Deiss., BS, 229; LAE, 110 f.; MM, s.v.); impers., ἀπέχει (Field, Notes, 39), it is enough: Mk 14:41.

