ἀληθής, -ές [  (&amp;lt; λήθω = λανθάνω, hence primarily, unconcealed, manifest; hence, actual, real),   [in LXX for אֶמֶת, etc.;] ]    (a) . of things, true, conforming to reality: Jo 4:18 5:31,32 6:55 (= ἀληθινός, q.v.) Jo 8:13,14, 17 10:41 19:35 21:24, Ac 12:9, Phl 4:8, Tit 1:13, I Pe 5:12, II Pe 2:22, I Jo 2:8, III Jo 12; 
